WEBVTT

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:14.030
So, what kind of research are
they doing here to have thieves break in?

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.800
Atmospheric continuum mechanics.

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:24.000
What is that, exactly?

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.170
This is a research facility for a company
that compresses air and sells it.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:37.300
You mean like oxygen tanks?
What would anyone be after here?

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.820
Are you all right? What happened here?

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:01.290
What the...? These are no ordinary thieves.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:04.960
Get back!

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:20.590
What was that?

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.140
It's frozen? Someone's ability?

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.110
No...

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.100
Hey!

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:32.950
They cut up the floor.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.070
Did they connect with the subways?

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.360
They got away.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.000
--Good morning!
--Good morning!

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:02.220
Early this morning,

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:06.350
the atmospheric continuum mechanics
research facility in School District 4

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:11.940
was broken into, and experimental
equipment was stolen.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.020
Tch.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:53.940
"#01 Accelerator
(Academy City's Mightiest Esper)"

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.490
"There you are!

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:09.620
You can't be outside when
it's well past your checkup time!"

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:13.360
says Misaka Misaka, criticizing you.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:19.050
"What's more, today's the big day
when your head bandages come off,"

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.880
says Misaka Misaka--

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:23.470
This isn't a holiday or anything like it.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:24.390
Huh?!

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:30.350
"It is a holiday! It is a holiday!

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:35.150
A holiday! A holiday!
A precious, important, not-to-be-missed,

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.320
significant, momentous day to remember!"

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:40.570
asserts Misaka Misaka in a loud voice!

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.570
Yeah, all right, all right.

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:46.280
Holiday! Holiday! Holiday! Holiday! Holiday!

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.850
Hmm, your wound is just about all closed up.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:54.670
You don't need the bandages anymore.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.090
Now, next up,

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.710
I have to do a simple examination.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:01.470
Don't need one.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:05.340
That bullet to your head
has caused some brain damage.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:10.980
It will have mainly affected your
speech, numerical, and motor skills.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:15.350
But there is still a lot we
don't know about the brain.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:18.980
Under certain circumstances,
this could prove life-threatening to you.

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:20.730
Are you threatening me?

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:25.110
I just want to provide the
best care for my patient that I can.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:26.110
Tch.

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:29.830
What is your name and background?

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:32.120
Accelerator.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:37.950
Once first-ranked among seven
Level 5 espers in Academy City.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:42.800
My ability is controlling all vectors,
like momentum, heat, and electricity.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:46.640
At one time, I took part
in Project Level 6 Shift, and,

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:53.480
as a result, I have to rely on this piece
of junk to be able to walk and talk right,

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:57.230
ending up a basket case, which
brings us up to today. That about cover it?

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:00.360
Hmm, no problems there, I'd say.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:05.150
Nice sense of sarcasm you got there.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.690
Ah, some other Misakas!

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.790
What is the matter, Last Order?

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:18.500
"Is the bandage-removal-celebration
party coming along okay?"

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:22.760
verifies Misaka Misaka,
unable to contain her eager heart.

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:28.680
"Readiness status is relayed among us
clones via the Misaka Network,"

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:30.890
says Misaka, expressing some doubt.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:36.640
"I know that, but this is my first
time throwing a party for someone,

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.270
so I can't help but check,"
says Misaka Misaka...

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:41.860
After all, today is--

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:46.550
Huh? What are you doing?

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:48.780
Nuh'ing.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:02.800
Antiskill. I need to see whoever's
in charge of the hospital.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:03.500
O-Okay.

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:13.180
If you all, who keep Academy City safe,
show up in full tactical gear,

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:14.900
can I assume you aren't here for a checkup?

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.980
I'd feel a lot better if we were.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:19.690
How's the chest wound coming along?

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:23.240
Coming to visit a sick friend
while you're at it? I'm coming along fine.

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:24.940
So, what's happened?

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:32.040
Early this morning, a research lab
in School District 4 was hit by thieves.

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:35.870
Apparently, it's a facility 
that researches air,

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.960
but behind the scenes, they were
also developing a secret weapon.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:40.460
That's what got stolen.

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:41.790
A secret weapon?

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:46.010
The facility has declined
to provide us with any specific data.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:50.550
If they can refuse to share
information with Antiskill,

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:51.760
they must be involved 
with the governing board.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.030
Yeah, they must be.

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:57.180
From what I've seen,
it's something like a water cutter,

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:59.100
which can slice through just about anything.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:03.440
So, how are the thieves who stole
this secret weapon connected to this place?

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:07.150
After checking into
similar research in the database,

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:12.480
it seems that the stolen secret weapon
is for use against Accelerator.

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:17.200
Indeed, that's something
I'll bet the governing board would want.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:21.290
This all means that the thieves
who have this secret weapon

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:23.630
are probably coming here, aren't they?

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:26.010
My read is that it's a good possibility.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:27.350
Still,

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:31.640
your numbers are pretty small
if you mean to intercept them here, huh?

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:36.430
When news reached the VIPs
that a secret weapon had been stolen,

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:38.350
they started carrying on
about being the targets,

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:40.430
and are monopolizing most of our personnel.

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:42.900
More worried about themselves
than some hospital?

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:46.860
That's some prize-winning corruption.
I wish they <i>would</i> go over there.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:53.700
Listen up, Accelerator!
It's time for your radical operation!

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:58.410
Sounds like they're here.

00:07:58.790 --> 00:07:59.360
Ito!

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:06.750
Excuse me, but could you
call Accelerator down for me?

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:08.590
I know he's here.

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:10.960
I'm afraid we can't honor that request.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:13.300
Put down the weapon
and surrender yourselves at once.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:18.720
By the book, huh?
Oh well. If you won't page him...

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:21.480
...I'll just have to...

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:23.510
...do it myself!

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:30.280
Fire!

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:38.370
Everyone, fall back!

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:42.500
--Emergency! Emergency!
Armed intruders in the hospital!

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:43.580
--Why aren't you taking shelter?
--Emergency! Emergency!
Armed intruders in the hospital!

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:43.910
--Why aren't you taking shelter?
--All patients, please follow staff
instructions and take immediate shelter!

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:45.710
--You hear the announcement, right?
--All patients, please follow staff
instructions and take immediate shelter!

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:47.330
--So what if I do?
--All patients, please follow staff
instructions and take immediate shelter!

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.630
--These thieves are apparently after you.
--All patients, please follow staff
instructions and take immediate shelter!

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:53.630
They stole a secret weapon that's
being developed with you in mind.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:54.730
Oh, they did?

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:59.560
Then again, while you're still probably okay,

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:02.470
they're likely to turn the
whole hospital upside down, so...

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:03.150
Huh?!

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:08.560
"If they turn the hospital upside down,
that includes the kitchen, right?"

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:10.680
says Misaka Misaka,
running off to ensure the ca--

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:14.780
to ensure that <i>they</i> are moved to safety.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:15.530
Hey!

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:19.820
I'll keep Last Order safe.
You hurry up and get out of here.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:24.370
Tch.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:35.800
Oh, Accelerator!

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:40.000
Look, that won't work.

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:46.140
Damn, being that bulletproof and
with a blade that sharp, what do we do?

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:46.970
They're coming through!

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:56.630
Come on, where's Accelerator?

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:00.740
Tch.

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:04.800
Hiro.

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:13.500
Okay, what will it be?

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:14.700
Yomikawa...

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:15.930
What is it?

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:18.620
That man behind the armed girl--

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:22.050
it looks like he's the one carrying
the magazines for that weapon.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:26.430
What if we went after him,
and then push her to use up her ammo?

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:28.770
Not bad. But who are they?

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:30.650
I've determined the culprits' identities.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:32.310
Takata Yoko.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:33.650
Kidera Minori.

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:36.990
Nakahara Hiromi.
All three are high school students.

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:41.070
They're just children, all right.

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:42.620
Which means you don't want to shoot them.

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:44.570
That's that, then.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:50.710
It's not my way to point guns at children.

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:54.460
Huh? You're radical. So, what will you do?

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:55.960
I'm just gonna do <i>this</i>!

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:56.970
Radical!

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:14.940
Well, aren't you radical?

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:19.160
No killing.

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:20.810
Tch.

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:25.330
"I went through trial and tribulation
all morning to make these,

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:25.330
"Kitchen"

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:26.660
and here are the fruits of my labor.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:33.330
I can't afford to lose these,"
mutters Misaka Misaka to herself.

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:37.300
Are they really that important?
Is this some kind of holiday?

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:42.260
Yes, today is an important day. It's his...

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:44.940
So...

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:48.130
Okay, let's take that and get to shelter.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:50.140
What about him?

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:51.480
I'm sure he's already gotten out.

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:56.770
"You told him to run away?"
questions Misaka Misaka.

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:57.370
Yes.

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:04.080
"That might have the opposite effect,"
says Misaka Misaka, worried about him.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:07.020
Are you okay?

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:09.450
I'm fine.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:12.040
Hey, fall back! We have to regroup.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:14.670
What? You're falling back again?

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:18.050
Hey, can't you mess with their density?

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:22.630
N-No, my ability only has
a range of about three meters.

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:24.420
That's seriously lame.

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:25.760
Sorry.

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:28.880
Yomikawa!

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:31.410
We can't go any farther.

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:43.810
We can't fall back any longer.

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:46.820
What's that? You're not falling back again?

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:51.290
Does that mean you're
all ready to get carved up?

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:55.290
Ito, Takahashi,
we'll take all three of them together.

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:58.000
What are you nattering on about?

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:02.690
The plan is for all three of us to go,
and whoever isn't cut up stops her?

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:05.970
Then it doesn't matter
which one of us she goes after.

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:09.810
What was that?! How radical!

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:12.270
I can slice through all
three of you, no problem!

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:21.110
Hiro!

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:24.750
Damn, man.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:34.160
You keep raising a racket right next
to my bedroom. Knock it off!

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:39.980
I get it. You must be Accelerator, right?

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:44.470
Are you the one who's
trying to pick a fight with me?

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:48.720
If you can break through a wall
to come at me, you're pretty radical, huh?

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:51.040
I've been anxious to meet you!

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:00.270
Doesn't look like defeating
you is going to be that simple.

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:04.150
Looks like defeating you
<i>is</i> gonna be that simple.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:05.740
"Ah, there you are!

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:09.620
I was worried that you didn't
get away, and went off to fight,"

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:14.810
says Misaka Misaka, sounding
like she's your guardian for once.

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:16.800
Wait!

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:22.290
Tch.

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:30.840
"That startled me.
I wasn't expecting the ceiling to collapse,"

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:34.860
says Misaka Misaka, unable to
conceal her shaking from this surprise.

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:39.850
You're hurt. Did you get hit by the rubble?

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:42.520
Nothing hit me.
I haven't had any action in a while,

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:44.020
and my wound opened back up, that's all.

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:46.190
Yes! That's blood!

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:50.070
Ah! N-No! H-Huh...?

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:52.810
Don't take me so lightly.

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:57.500
Maybe I should take a little bit
more genetic material with me!

00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:00.920
Don't do it, Yo!
You don't have to take things this far!

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:01.910
Tch.

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:06.350
Well, radical. Let's go.
Take one of Hiro's magazines.

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:09.220
Huh? We're leaving Hiro here?

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:11.760
Don't talk back, just do it, Kidera.

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:15.890
S-Sorry.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:16.640
Let's go.

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:23.900
They got away. Check our status.

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:26.150
The children are all clear.

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:28.210
Good. Secure the boy.

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:29.450
--Anyone who can keep up,
we're going after them.

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:30.400
--What was that bag?
--Anyone who can keep up,
we're going after them.

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:31.740
--It's...
--Yes, ma'am.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:32.390
--Huh?
--Yes, ma'am.

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:35.120
Never mind about the bag,

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:38.550
Misaka Misaka is more
worried about your injury.

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:39.700
Tch.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:43.500
Damn it, what's the use?

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:46.460
If you're going after 
them, we'll take my car.

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:47.450
Don't need it.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:51.340
Shouldn't you preserve
your battery as much as you can?

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:52.930
Can you even drive?

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:57.120
You took a gunshot to the chest,
and your bandages aren't even off yet.

00:15:57.720 --> 00:16:00.390
If I rupture a blood vessel,
will you reconnect it for me?

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:02.580
Not on your life.

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:10.030
You really do go to great 
lengths for that girl.

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:13.200
I just can't stand having those
punks getting the better of me.

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:15.570
They did get away
with your genetic data, too.

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:20.450
She really does think the world of you.
That's why she spent so much time--

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:22.190
Huh?

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:25.460
Anyhow, where should we go?

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:28.380
Standard villain theory says
that they'll first go underground,

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:30.550
to avoid any satellite surveillance.

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:34.180
"School District 7
underground drainage channel"

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:33.130
There's an underground sewer near here.

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:34.550
Then that's the place.

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:36.400
Underground again.

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:38.510
Let's look for another entrance.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:44.810
Listen, Yo...

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:45.870
Huh?

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:49.780
Do you think they caught Hiro?

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:52.280
Ugh, are you still on that?

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:54.630
If you're that concerned,
why don't you go help him on your own?

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:55.740
I couldn't.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:17:01.590
That stuff you're carrying is
radical first-ranked genetic data.

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:06.580
We take that to the right lab and
play our cards right, and we're billionaires.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:10.550
Once we have that, we'll think
of some backdoor way to rescue Hiro.

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:13.050
But first, we have to make
a clean getaway, right?

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:16.580
Then why are you doing that?

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:19.500
I want to make sure
we give any pursuers the slip.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:23.980
Or did you really think we can get
away clean with you along, slowpoke?

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.850
Then why not just bring
an end to everything right here?

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:31.110
What are you talking about?

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:34.270
You can't even get close to me.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:46.920
Super-radical! That was way beyond radical!

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:53.630
Radical! How are you not hurt?!

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:56.220
Disappointed, are you?

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:00.220
The cat's out of the bag about your weapon.

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:05.020
Nitrogen, right?
That last explosion employed nitrogen,

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:07.730
which turns solid at
anything under -210 degrees.

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:12.400
So your little toy is actually
an ultra-high-pressure water cutter,

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:14.850
which uses the melting of solid nitrogen.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:20.370
But the clincher is using the
unseen nitrogen that gets spread about

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:22.910
to deprive anyone
who gets too close of oxygen.

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:24.830
Get your filthy hand off of me.

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:26.330
You got it!

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:32.750
I'm surprised you thought
you could get at me with such a trinket.

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:36.800
Now then, how come you guys,
who are standing in the middle of the nitrogen

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:40.390
don't get deprived of oxygen?
It's because of <i>you</i>,

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:43.350
someone who's way too unsteady
to just be carrying the goods.

00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:47.230
You're able to control
the concentration of gases in the air--

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:49.340
something of an aero-separator, right?

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:53.900
You maintain enough breathable
air around you and your pals.

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:56.820
But now that I know about it, you're done.

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:59.570
You see, my ability
to manipulate any kind of vector

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:02.370
is upwardly compatible to yours!

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:10.870
I've now revealed all your tricks.

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:17.590
Fine, just let us have your genetic data.
Don't be so stingy!

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:22.640
Don't even bother.
I'm not like that preachy Level 0.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.970
If you want to keep going,
I won't hold back anymore.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:29.390
Your blood will be mine!!

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:31.840
Radical!

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:38.490
Yo!

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:41.990
Well? Do you want to still keep going?

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:43.870
No! You're going to kill Yo!

00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:47.620
If you want to keep fighting,
I-I'll take you on.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:50.750
Huh?

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:56.290
Tch.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:04.010
If she's so important to you
that you'd risk your life,

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:07.100
you should have stopped
her before she did all of this.

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:13.690
Earlier today, at around noon,

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:17.570
the trio who attacked a hospital
in School District 7 were arrested.

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:20.650
--The three suspects in this case 
also stole a weapon under development

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:20.650
--"Ah! Thank you!" declares
Misaka Misaka, full of gratitude!

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:21.780
--from an atmospheric continuum 
mechanics research facility...

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:21.780
--"Ah! Thank you!" declares
Misaka Misaka, full of gratitude!

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:22.990
--from an atmospheric continuum
mechanics research facility...

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:22.990
--Shut up.

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:27.410
"Huh?" says Misaka Misaka,
making her discontent known.

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:29.450
So, what is that, exactly, anyway?

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:35.580
"If you really want to know,
I would be willing to reveal it to you,"

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:38.250
says Misaka Misaka, resisting
the impulse to show you outright,

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:40.590
and acting a little pretentious.

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:42.840
Then never mind. I'm not all that interested.

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:44.970
"I'm kidding, I'm kidding!
Have a look, have a look!"

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:49.390
says Misaka Misaka, putting aside
her games and giving this to you!

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:51.240
Open it up.

00:20:56.440 --> 00:21:00.360
"We're just getting started"

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:05.490
"There's still lots of party
left to celebrate your recovery,

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:07.450
so be looking forward to tonight,"

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:10.370
says Misaka Misaka,
making an official announcement.

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:12.150
Rubbish.

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:17.250
"Ah! No, no!
It won't work unless you're here,

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:19.590
so make sure you come
tonight when I call you,"

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:22.730
says Misaka Misaka, pleading with you
and not worrying about spoiling anything!

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:45.530
"A Certain Scientific Accelerator"

00:23:08.820 --> 00:23:10.450
Don't try to resist.

00:23:28.970 --> 00:23:31.130
This is where you are.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:37.010
"Next time"

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:41.570
"Necromancer"
